# Commit at milestones (HARD)

Shopify draft `187144929571` is **QA runtime only**. GitHub / `shopify-build/` is Design System master.

## When to remind (same turn, one short line)

Remind Andrew **once** to commit (or hold) when any of these happen:

1. He says **looks good / approved / lock it / freeze** for a section or PDP beat
2. A named Liquid/CSS/asset fix is pushed to draft **and** he confirms visually
3. OS / slogan / Type OS docs change in `planning/` or `manychat-kb/`
4. Switching to a **new surface** (Home → Shop All → another PDP → SEO) after work on the prior one
5. End of a dense QA session (multiple approved tweaks still only on draft / local dirty tree)

## What to say

- What’s dirty (Liquid vs JSON vs docs)
- Draft is ahead of GitHub if true
- Ask: commit now, or keep holding until the next named batch
- Never auto-commit unless he explicitly says to commit in that message

## Do not

- Treat Theme Editor / draft alone as “saved to the OS”
- Dump `templates/*.json` / `settings_data.json` into a commit without a draft pull + his named file approval
- Nag every tiny nudge — milestones only
- Touch live theme `185687998755`

